<div class="panel-inner">
  <h2 class="panel-title">About Me</h2>

  <div class="about-layout">
    <div class="about-body">
      <p>
        I'm Ofer — a technology and product professional working at the intersection of
        technology, information systems, business processes, and user needs. I enjoy
        understanding how things work, identifying what people actually need, and
        turning complex requirements into practical, well-designed solutions.
      </p>
      <p>
        My professional experience includes leading large-scale information system
        projects, particularly national Spatial Data Infrastructure (SDI) initiatives
        in Zanzibar and Nigeria. These projects have given me hands-on experience
        across the full product and system lifecycle — from understanding business
        processes and gathering user requirements to working with developers on
        system design, managing implementation, and supporting adoption. A big part
        of my role is connecting the technical side with the people and organizations
        that ultimately use the systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also bring a strong analytical background. My research-based Master's
        degree from Tel Aviv University focused on urban mobility, where I conducted
        a quantitative analysis of over one million shared e-scooter trips to
        investigate how cycling infrastructure influences travel behaviour. The
        research involved large-scale data processing and analysis using Python,
        GIS, spatial and transport network analysis, and statistical methods.
        It strengthened my ability to work with complex datasets, approach problems
        systematically, and translate data into meaningful insights.
      </p>
      <p>
        Alongside my professional work, I've been expanding my technical skills
        in AI and large language models, experimenting with AI agents, tool
        integrations, and practical applications of these technologies to
        real-world problems.
      </p>
      <p>
        Looking ahead, I want to continue growing in roles that combine a solid
        understanding of technology with business and operational thinking.
        I'm particularly interested in the space between technical teams,
        products, and users — where understanding both what technology can do
        and what a business actually needs makes the biggest difference.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="about-sidebar">
      <div class="skills-section">
        <h3 class="skills-title">Programming</h3>
        <div class="chips">
          <span class="chip">Python</span>
          <span class="chip">SQL</span>
